  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ndpi_search_kerberos",
    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/protocols/kerberos.c",
    "description": "In the AS-REQ parsing path, `name_offset` is advanced based on several ASN.1 heuristics, but then `cname_len = packet->payload[name_offset];` is read without re-validating that `name_offset < packet->payload_packet_len`. Earlier checks only ensure `name_offset < payload_len - 1` before subsequent increments (`name_offset += 1`, optional `name_offset++`, optional `name_offset += 2`), so `name_offset` can become exactly `payload_len` and cause a 1-byte OOB read. This is the direct missing-bounds-check bug (crash at kerberos.c:501).",
    "conditions": "Triggered via `fuzz_process_packet` calling `ndpi_detection_process_packet` on attacker-controlled packet bytes. Input must be parsed as Kerberos AS-REQ (`msg_type == 0x0A`) and reach the cname extraction block where `name_offset` is near the end of the payload; crafted bytes make the optional offset-adjustment branches fire so `name_offset` is incremented past the last valid byte before reading `packet->payload[name_offset]`. The provided PoC packet (157 bytes) satisfies these conditions and causes heap-buffer-overflow read at the end of the fuzz buffer."
  },
